@Alexi5000 good catch, i missed the string-array case, fixed in [c9f6db7e](https://github.com/decolua/9router/commit/c9f6db7e02367da74cb360506dc50b2fbcb983ac)

kept this scoped to the FLUX.2 multipart path: string/mixed arrays and invalid bytes now return 400, as does nonempty or malformed `images`, before any fetch. `images: []` and `null` remain no-ops, and legacy JSON handling is unchanged

added regression coverage for both cases and byte validation: 16 failures on the previous commit, now 36/36 in this suite and 65/65 across the three focused suites, all offline with mocked DNS/fetch

